        img: null,
        google: { rating: 2.6, review_count: 11, maps_url: 'https://maps.google.com/?cid=12015740341528526238&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA', reviews: [{author: 'Mage Michelle', rating: 1, text: 'It’s unfortunate I have to write this review, because I do love the doctor and most of the staff. There are a couple desk staff at the Albert Lea location that have refused to figure out the communication issue between their office and my insurance provider, and they have been completely condescending towards me about it. I’ve had coverage with Eyemed(one of Innovisions covered providers) for over', time: '7 years ago'}, {author: 'fiery katy', rating: 1, text: 'I really did not enjoy my time here....I will be taking my business elsewhere. The nurse on the phone was super condescending, the doctor didn’t communicate much about my concerns that I told the nurse about, and the only time one of the nurses seemed even remotely nice was when they noticed I was upset. If you know somebody struggles with mental health disorders, maybe you should take the time as', time: '6 years ago'}, {author: 'C Nagel', rating: 1, text: 'My experience is the same as the people that have responded below.  They are just -very rude- people.  Guess they just have to much business.  Don\'t spend the time to respond to this because its clear that you are not fixing your problems and I won\'t be back.   I\'ll take my business out of a local downtown business and go to Walmart.', time: '6 years ago'}, {author: 'Shawn Davis', rating: 1, text: 'The doctor was fine. The billing was horrendous and they\'ve gone round and round with my elderly mother over $30 due to creative billing. Avoid.', time: '5 years ago'}, {author: 'Jeremy Peak', rating: 1, text: '$200 for an eye exam is ridiculous. Three time more than many places. I have to go here for safety glasses through work, but I won\'t go here for another exam or any other glasses again. Seriously unhappy.', time: '6 years ago'}] }
